The goal is to keep `readOnlyRootFilesystem: true` and fix the crash by allowing necessary writes using volumes.

Nginx often writes to `/var/log/nginx` (logs) and might use temporary directories. I will add a writable `emptyDir` volume and mount it to both `/var/log` and `/var/cache` to cover common failure points while maintaining the read-only root.

I will construct a strategic merge patch to add the volume mount configuration to the container spec.

Patch structure:
1. Add `volumes` section under `spec.template.spec`.
2. Add `volumeMounts` section to the `app` container spec, pointing to the new volume and desired paths.

The patch needs to target the `app` container.

Patch:
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "volumes": [
          {
            "name": "data-vol"
          }
        ],
        "containers": [
          {
            "name": "app",
            "volumeMounts": [
              {
                "name": "data-vol",
                "mountPath": "/var/log"
              },
              {
                "name": "data-vol",
                "mountPath": "/var/cache"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
